# gen/go is buf generate output. It is committed because Go modules distribute
# source: without it, `go build ./...` on a fresh clone fails until someone
# installs the buf toolchain and regenerates, and gopls knows none of the
# symbols until they do. `make proto-check` is what keeps it from drifting out
# of step with proto/.
#
# What it should not do is behave like hand-written code in review.

# Collapses these files in GitHub diffs and leaves them out of the language
# statistics, so a one-line proto change does not open as a 500-line review.
gen/go/** linguist-generated=true

# Refuses a three-way merge rather than producing a file that is half of each
# branch's generated output and compiles by accident. Git keeps the current
# branch's version and declares a conflict; the resolution is always the same,
# and it is never to edit the file: run `make proto` and commit the result.
#
# There is deliberately no `-diff` here. That would render these as "Binary
# files differ" locally too, and the review noise it would save is already
# handled by linguist-generated above — leaving only the loss, which is being
# unable to see what a proto change actually did to the generated API.
gen/go/** -merge

# sqlc output, for the same reasons. The glob follows the out: path every
# sqlc.yaml entry is required to use, so a new service picks this up by putting
# its generated package where the others are rather than by editing this file.
services/*/internal/adapter/out/postgres/sqlc/** linguist-generated=true
services/*/internal/adapter/out/postgres/sqlc/** -merge
